# Exceptions for tools/kit-check: one `path<TAB>string` per line, separated by a single tab.
# A hit in `path` passes only when an occurrence of `string` in the same line covers the matched text.
# For commit metadata, `path` is `@ident` or `@message`. Keep every entry exact; never allow a bare name.
# The repository's own URL has to appear where the kit tells people how to install it.
README.md	aiongg/craft-ui-port-kit
.claude-plugin/plugin.json	aiongg/craft-ui-port-kit
.claude-plugin/marketplace.json	aiongg/craft-ui-port-kit
skills/craft-ui-port/SKILL.md	aiongg/craft-ui-port-kit
tools/scip/scip_pb2.py	from google.protobuf.internal import builder as _builder
tools/land/rewrite-rules.txt	regex:/Users/[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9._-]*/==>/path/to/local/
tools/land/rewrite-rules.txt	regex:/tmp/claude-[^\s"'`)\]>,;]*==>/tmp/scratch
# The one commit is authored by the repository owner's GitHub noreply address.
@ident	aiongg <67543387+aiongg@users.noreply.github.com>
# Selftest commits in scratch repos use a reserved, non-routable address.
tools/selftest/lib.py	selftest@example.invalid
